MR. KIRCHNER","x":"Oh, okay, that was '36?"},{"p":29,"b":6,"s":"MR. SAUTER","x":"Yes. That was the Chicago."},{"p":29,"b":7,"s":"MR. SAUTER","x":"I think the Commodore Hotel in New York was the first job; they went to Boston, Syracuse. All the time I was playing trumpet until the Black Hawk, and writing."},{"p":29,"b":8,"s":"MR. KIRCHNER","x":"When did he decide to make the jump into having a big band?"},{"p":30,"b":0,"s":"MR. SAUTER","x":"He must have been considering it, but I'm sure it happened--"},{"p":30,"b":1,"s":"","x":"(Side A of Tape 1 ended at this point. Transcript will continue with Side B.)"},{"p":31,"b":0,"s":"","x":"(Side B of Tape 1 begins at this point.)"},{"p":31,"b":1,"s":"MR. SAUTER","x":"--that last winter, '35 and '36. That's when Benny had started to hit it. Who else? I guess the Dorsey Brothers. Bob Crosby too. Artie Shaw."}]}